{
 "lines": [
  {
   "id": "VO-01",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 6.12,
   "text": "G T A six drops tomorrow. Millions will buy the game, but some people own the company that makes it."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-02",
   "start": 6.4,
   "end": 7.94,
   "text": "Wait, who owns GTA?"
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-03",
   "start": 8.24,
   "end": 10.42,
   "text": "Take-Two, Rockstar's parent company."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-04",
   "start": 10.64,
   "end": 17.5,
   "text": "Put a thousand dollars into Take-Two the day G T A five came out in twenty thirteen, and you'd have about thirteen thousand today."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-05",
   "start": 18.0,
   "end": 21.74,
   "text": "That's far more than the S and P five hundred did over the same years."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-06",
   "start": 21.96,
   "end": 26.16,
   "text": "And G T A five helped Take-Two nearly double its revenue in one year."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-07",
   "start": 26.66,
   "end": 33.52,
   "text": "But here's what most people miss: the stock had already run from about eleven dollars to eighteen before G T A five launched."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-08",
   "start": 33.74,
   "end": 38.48,
   "text": "Today it jumped about seven percent, so some of the hype may already be priced in."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-09",
   "start": 38.68,
   "end": 44.42,
   "text": "Bank of America's price target is three hundred thirty dollars, while the lowest analyst target is one seventy."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-10",
   "start": 45.22,
   "end": 48.68,
   "text": "So tomorrow, are you buying the game, the stock, or both?"
  }
 ],
